  <h2>A traditional barbershop shave</h2>
  <p>A hot-towel straight-razor shave is a different appointment from shortening a beard. It focuses on a close finish rather than maintaining the length of your facial hair. Tell your barber what you want to remove and whether you intend to keep a mustache or other facial hair.</p>
  <h2>Shave or beard trim?</h2>
  <p>If you want to keep your beard and tidy its shape, choose our <a href="/beard-trim-richmond-va">beard trim service</a>. If you want a close shave, look for Hot Towel Shave in the booking menu. Call us if you are unsure which option matches your plans.</p>
  <h2>Planning your appointment</h2>
  <p>Appointments are recommended. Check the available services and times before visiting, especially if you also want a haircut. Let your barber know about your usual shaving routine and any concerns you want to discuss before the service begins.</p>
  <p>Browse <a href="/mens-haircut-richmond-va">men's haircuts</a> to plan the rest of your visit.</p>
  <h2>Book a shave in Carytown</h2>
  <p>Our shop is at 2820 W Cary St, Suite C, Richmond, VA 23221. The booking menu shows current prices and available appointments; call the shop if you need help choosing a service.</p>
</ServiceDetailLayout>
